From: Liuqin Linux Kit maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Recovery ADSP independent of disabled audio PRM clocks

Recovery disables the GPR audio subtree while retaining ADSP for PMIC
battery and charging communication. The desktop's PRM clock child cannot
be instantiated from that disabled subtree; treating this as ENOMEM
prevents the entire ADSP from probing. Skip only this audio setup in the
explicit Recovery profile, preserving the shared board identity helper
and the normal desktop clock lifecycle.

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -982,6 +982,10 @@ static int liuqin_create_prm_clocks(struct qcom_pas *pas)
 	if (!liuqin_board_quirks() || !pas->info_name || strcmp(pas->info_name, "adsp"))
 		return 0;
 
+	/* Recovery retains ADSP charging services, but disables GPR audio. */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(of_root, "liuqin,recovery"))
+		return 0;
+
 	edge = of_get_child_by_name(pas->dev->of_node, "glink-edge");
 	gpr = of_get_compatible_child(edge, "qcom,gpr");
 	prm = of_get_compatible_child(gpr, "qcom,q6prm");
